Implemented and committed as `8b92483` on `feat/media-contribute-authority`.

### Root cause

Instrumentation showed there was no pre-existing registration. The test stub was used:

```text
provider_count: 1
provider: cms-akira-media
policy: NULL
origin.type: runtime_register
```

CI differs because `.env.ci` sets `APP_MULTI_TENANT_ENABLED=0`, while local sets it to `1`. In single-tenant mode, `CapabilityBus::applyPolicy()` calls implicit `moduleIsActive($pid)`, which requires global activation. The test only provisioned explicit tenant activation.

The captured log entries were:

```text
[2026-09-12 20:09:31] [warning] Capability provider 'cms-akira-media' skipped — module not active for tenant {"capability_id":"akira.media.upload@1","provider":"cms-akira-media","caller_module":"cms-akira-media","request_id":"3b2081d04375fa5d"}
[2026-09-12 20:09:31] [warning] capability.denied {"capability_id":"akira.media.upload@1","caller_module":"cms-akira-media","caller_user_id":999501,"reason":"caller_policy","request_id":"3b2081d04375fa5d","correlation_id":null}
```

The repair temporarily enables `cms-akira-media` globally in single-tenant mode, verifies implicit dispatch-scope activation, and restores `storage/modules.json` exactly afterward.

